-- title:
--   The maximal ideal of R[[X₁,…,Xₙ]] is (varpi,X₁,…,Xₙ)
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative local ring, let $n$ be a natural number, and let $\varpi$ be an element of $R$ whose principal ideal is exactly the maximal ideal of $R$, i.e. $\mathfrak{m}_R = (\varpi)$. Consider the multivariate formal power series ring $R[[X_i : i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,n]]$, i.e. $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,n, R)$, which is again a local ring. The assertion is that the ideal generated by the finite list consisting of the constant series $\mathrm{C}(\varpi)$ followed by the $n$ variables $X_0,\dots,X_{n-1}$ (the list obtained from the indexed family $X : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to R[[X_i]]$, the ideal being `Ideal.ofList` of that list, i.e. the span of its entries) coincides with the maximal ideal of $R[[X_i : i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,n]]$. Equivalently: a power series over $R$ in $n$ variables lies in the maximal ideal precisely when it can be written as $\varpi f_{-1} + \sum_{i} X_i f_i$ with power series coefficients $f_{-1}, f_0, \dots, f_{n-1}$. No hypothesis of Noetherianity, domain or discrete valuation is imposed beyond the principality of $\mathfrak m_R$; the number of variables is finite.
--
--   This is the standard description of the maximal ideal of a power series ring over a local ring with principal maximal ideal, in the form needed to exhibit $(\varpi, X_1,\dots,X_n)$ as a generating sequence. It is used in the patching argument, where $R$ is the ring of integers of a local field with uniformiser $\varpi$, to feed the sequence into freeness and kernel computations over $\mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$, as in [`Algebra.PatchingLevel.free_and_ker_eq_span`](thm.html#Algebra.PatchingLevel.free_and_ker_eq_span) and [`MvPowerSeries.exists_coords_of_quotient_span_finite_free`](thm.html#MvPowerSeries.exists_coords_of_quotient_span_finite_free).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_ofList_C_cons_X_eq_maximalIdeal.lean

import Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPowerSeries.Inverse
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Regular.RegularSequence

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

universe u

theorem MvPowerSeries.ofList_C_cons_X_eq_maximalIdeal {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    (n : ℕ) {ϖ : R} (hϖ : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {ϖ}) :
    Ideal.ofList (MvPowerSeries.C ϖ :: List.ofFn (MvPowerSeries.X : Fin n → MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R)) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R) := by sorry
